  "prompt": "/deep-research I am researching trends of young people leaving Wales. According to the Welsh Census 2021 and official Welsh government data, find the local authorities that did NOT see an overall decrease in amount of households since 2011. Out of these local authorities, identify those that had a population of less than 120,000 at the point of mid-year 2021 and are not in the North Wales region. From this selection, identify the all local authorities that have seen an increase of over 2% in people aged 25 to 44 between mid-year 2021 and mid-year 2022.",
  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "I am researching trends of young people leaving Wales. According to the Welsh Census 2021 and official Welsh government data, find the local authorities that did NOT see an overall decrease in amount of households since 2011. Out of these local authorities, identify those that had a population of less than 120,000 at the point of mid-year 2021 and are not in the North Wales region. From this selection, identify the all local authorities that have seen an increase of over 2% in people aged 25 to 44 between mid-year 2021 and mid-year 2022.",
  "answer": "Now I have all the research data. Let me compile and apply the filters step by step.\n\n**Step 1: Local authorities with NO household decrease (2011→2021)**\n19 of 22: All except Gwynedd, Ceredigion, Blaenau Gwent\n\n**Step 2: Population < 120,000 at mid-2021**\n9 authorities: Merthyr Tydfil, Blaenau Gwent, Isle of Anglesey, Ceredigion, Torfaen, Monmouthshire, Denbighshire, Conwy, Gwynedd\n\n**Step 3: Exclude North Wales (6 authorities: Isle of Anglesey, Conwy, Denbighshire, Flintshire, Gwynedd, Wrexham)**\nRemaining: Merthyr Tydfil, Blaenau Gwent, Ceredigion, Torfaen, Monmouthshire\n\n**Step 4: >2% increase in 25-44 age group (2021→2022)**\nFrom the 5 remaining:\n- Torfaen: 2.31% ✓\n- Monmouthshire: 2.82% ✓\n- Others: below 2% ✗\n\n---\n\n## Final Answer\n\n**Two Welsh local authorities meet all four criteria:**\n\n| Local Authority | Household Change 2011→2021 | Mid-2021 Pop | Region | 25-44 Pop 2021 | 25-44 Pop 2022 | % Change 25-44 |\n|----------------|---------------------------|--------------|--------|----------------|----------------|----------------|\n| **Torfaen** | +1,676 (+4.4%) | 92,453 | South East Wales | 23,043 | 23,576 | **+2.31%** |\n| **Monmouthshire** | +2,667 (+7.0%) | 93,194 | South East Wales | 19,236 | 19,778 | **+2.82%** |\n\n### Verification against all criteria:\n\n| Criterion | Torfaen | Monmouthshire |\n|-----------|---------|---------------|\n| 1. No household decrease (2011→2021) | ✓ (+4.4%) | ✓ (+7.0%) |\n| 2. Population < 120,000 (mid-2021) | ✓ (92,453) | ✓ (93,194) |\n| 3. Not in North Wales | ✓ (South East) | ✓ (South East) |\n| 4. >2% increase 25-44 (2021→2022) | ✓ (2.31%) | ✓ (2.82%) |\n\n---\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] ONS Census 2021 household estimates — Figure 6 data download: https://www.ons.gov.uk/visualisations/dvc1915/fig6/datadownload.xlsx\n\n[2] ONS Mid-2021 Population Estimates (MYE2 - Persons worksheet): https://www.ons.gov.uk/file?uri=/peoplepopulationandcommunity/populationandmigration/populationestimates/datasets/populationestimatesforukenglandandwalesscotlandandnorthernireland/mid2021/ukpopestimatesmid2021on2021geographyfinal.xls\n\n[3] Senedd Research — North Wales Corporate Joint Committee definition (6 authorities): https://research.senedd.wales/research-articles/collaboration-nation-what-are-corporate-joint-committees-and-what-will-they-do\n\n[4] ONS Detailed time series MYEB1 (2021 Geography) — 25-44 age band 2021 vs 2022: https://www.ons.gov.uk/file?uri=/peoplepopulationandcommunity/populationandmigration/populationestimates/datasets/estimatesofthepopulationforenglandandwales/mid2011tomid2022detailedtimeseries/myebtablesenglandwales20112022v2.xlsx\n\n[5] ONS Mid-2022 Population Estimates (2021 boundaries) — 25-44 verification: https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/populationandmigration/populationestimates/datasets/estimatesofthepopulationforenglandandwales/mid20222021localauthorityboundaires",
  "answer_chars": 2859,
